Here is an example of a C++ condition that checks if the minimum angle value is no greater than -180 and the maximum value is no greater than 180:
```
if (angle >= -180 && angle <= 180) {
  // angle is within the acceptable range
} else {
  // angle is outside the acceptable range
}
```
Alternatively, you can use the `std::limits` header to check the minimum and maximum values of the type of `angle`:
```
if (std::numeric_limits<decltype(angle)>::min() <= angle && angle <= std::numeric_limits<decltype(angle)>::max()) {
  // angle is within the acceptable range
} else {
  // angle is outside the acceptable range
}
```

